cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Fly Simulator, please cite it as below. If you use the connectome brain
  model, please also cite the FlyWire papers (Dorkenwald et al. 2024; Schlegel et al.
  2024) and Shiu et al. 2024, and for the body NeuroMechFly v2 (Wang-Chen et al. 2024).
  See NOTICE.md for the full list.
title: "Fly Simulator"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jayden
    family-names: Lin
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NewYorkImperialist/fly-simulator"
url: "https://github.com/NewYorkImperialist/fly-simulator"
abstract: >-
  A physically simulated fruit fly (NeuroMechFly on FlyGym 2.x / MuJoCo) that walks
  through endless procedural terrain, driven in part by a whole-brain leaky
  integrate-and-fire model of the FlyWire v783 connectome (after Shiu et al. 2024).
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - NeuroMechFly
  - MuJoCo
  - simulation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dorkenwald
        given-names: Sven
      - name: "The FlyWire Consortium"
    journal: Nature
    volume: 634
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07558-y
  - type: article
    title: "Whole-brain annotation and multi-connectome cell typing of Drosophila"
    authors:
      - family-names: Schlegel
        given-names: Philipp
    journal: Nature
    volume: 634
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07686-5
  - type: article
    title: "A Drosophila computational brain model reveals sensorimotor processing"
    authors:
      - family-names: Shiu
        given-names: Philip K.
    journal: Nature
    volume: 634
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9
  - type: article
    title: "NeuroMechFly v2: simulating embodied sensorimotor control in adult Drosophila"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wang-Chen
        given-names: Sibo
    journal: Nature Methods
    volume: 21
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41592-024-02497-y
